WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.750
In tutorial 9.2, you'll read your
backlinks, and find where to get more.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.695
First, open Backlinks.

00:00:13.745 --> 00:00:17.145
The alerts at the top tell you
what changed since the last check,

00:00:17.195 --> 00:00:18.899
like a link that was removed.

00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:24.243
Below, you see how many sites link to
you, how many links are new or lost,

00:00:24.293 --> 00:00:27.004
and your best links,
each checked on its page.

00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:30.752
The spam score watches
for low-quality links,

00:00:30.802 --> 00:00:34.042
and Visits from links counts
the people those links send you.

00:00:35.087 --> 00:00:40.362
Next, scroll to Links. Best shows the links
worth the most, with a value for each,

00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:42.198
and whether it's still on the page.

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:46.218
Click Lost to see the
links you lost, and why.

00:00:46.268 --> 00:00:50.261
A link counts as lost only after
it's missing from its page twice.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:55.205
The other tabs show every link, new
links, links that send you visits,

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.396
and spammy ones.

00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:01.741
Further down, Anchor texts shows
the words sites use to link to you,

00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:05.176
and Your most-linked pages
shows where those links land.

00:01:06.175 --> 00:01:09.240
Then, Opportunities shows
where to get more links.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.967
Unlinked mentions are sites that
name you, but don't link to you.

00:01:13.951 --> 00:01:16.876
Competitors' new links shows
who just linked to them,

00:01:16.926 --> 00:01:21.040
and Link gap shows sites that link
to your competitors, but not to you.

00:01:21.989 --> 00:01:25.914
Click Best of lists to see list
pages that name your competitors,

00:01:25.964 --> 00:01:27.205
and whether you're on them.

00:01:29.035 --> 00:01:33.430
Finally, the Outreach pipeline ranks
the sites worth asking for a link.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.867
Click Outreach e-mail on a prospect.

00:01:36.872 --> 00:01:41.072
You see why they're worth it, who
to write to, and a drafted e-mail.

00:01:41.122 --> 00:01:43.834
Click Open in mail to send
it from your own e-mail.

00:01:44.851 --> 00:01:47.851
Once you've sent it,
click Mark as contacted.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:52.687
It moves to the Contacted tab, where you
follow up and see who replied or linked.

00:01:53.686 --> 00:01:57.161
Now you know which links you won
or lost, which are worth the most,

00:01:57.211 --> 00:01:58.574
and who to ask next.

00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:05.288
Want the list somewhere else? Download
prospects.csv at the top of the page.

00:02:06.287 --> 00:02:10.337
So, read what's new and lost,
filter to your best or lost links,

00:02:10.387 --> 00:02:13.154
see your opportunities,
and contact a prospect.

00:02:14.208 --> 00:02:18.505
Next, add the links Google
knows about, in tutorial 9.3.
